Translation patch: combinators in packets/mod.rs and row/mod.rs (`OkPacket::{into_owned, info_ref, session_state_info_ref}`, `ServerError::sql_state_ref`, `MyDeserialize` for `ErrPacket`, `NullBitmap`, `RowDeserializer<_, Binary>`)

Change: These become explicit `match`es (with `return Err(unexpected_buf_eof())` where the combinator was followed by `?`): `opt.map(|x| x.into_owned())`, `opt.as_ref().map(|x| x.as_bytes())`, `.map(ErrPacket::Progress)`, `.map(ErrPacket::Error)`, `self.state.as_ref()` and `.ok_or_else(unexpected_buf_eof)?`.
Why: The same as patch 09: Aeneas fails on closures and constructors used as values, and does not model `ok_or_else`. It does not model `Option::as_ref` either.
Behaviour: Identical: each `match` is the definition of the combinator.

